{
  "slug": "sextant",
  "name": "Sextant",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Sextant provides systematic, tiered workflows for common coding tasks — bug fixes, new features, refactoring, code review, test writing, and requirements refinement. Like a nautical sextant that helps navigators fix their exact position before charting a course, it helps Claude understand where it is in the codebase before making changes.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **13 skills** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (13): `add-feature` (You MUST use this skill before writing any code for a new feature, module, class, or API endpoint), `debug` (You MUST use this skill before reading any code or proposing any fix when the bug location is…), `fix-bug` (You MUST use this skill before writing any fix or editing any code to address a bug), `migrate` (You MUST use this skill before starting any cross-module migration, upgrade, or technology conversion), `modify-feature` (You MUST use this skill before changing, enhancing, or refactoring any existing functionality), `plan` (You MUST use this skill before starting multi-step implementation work when no ordered task breakdown exists yet), `principles` (Fallback for general coding work that does not match any specific sextant sub-skill), `refine-requirements` (You MUST use this skill before writing any design or code when the requirement is vague, ambiguous, or…), and 5 more\n- **Hooks** (1): `hooks.json`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install sextant@claude-community` from `hellotern/Sextant`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 13,
    "hook": 1
  },
